{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-inflammatory, anti-sepsis", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of the peptide shows 61.76% similarity to frog Cathelicidin-RC2. 12% S; 18% K. Mol Wt: 3673.395; GRAVY: -0.29; mol formula: C162H277N49O42S2. Activity: Active against E. coli ATCC25922 (MIC 10.2 uM), P. aeruginosa ATCC27853 (MIC 10.2 uM), H. pylori 26695 or 11637 (MIC 2.55 uM), and Gram+ S. aureus ATCC25923 (MIC 20.42 uM). Inactive: B.subtilis, E.faecalis, and S.epidermidis clinical strains (MIC >200 ug/ml) Anti-inflammatory: At 10 ug/mL, OL-CATH2 significantly inhibited the LPS-induced transcription and production of pro-inflammatory cytokines TNF-alpha, IL-1beta, and IL-6 in mouse peritoneal macrophages. Updated Jan2020; 7/2021; 11/2022", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "30127328", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Zool Res. 2019. 40 (2), 94-101. doi: 10.24272/j.issn.2095-8137.2018.062. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03012", "source_id": "AP03012", "source_numeric_id": "03012", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03012", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Identification and characterization of two novel cathelicidins from the frog Odorrana livida.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
